# BPO Superflow Pipeline — Latency Analysis

## Pipeline Architecture Overview

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["input_gatekeeper"] --> B["analyze_transcripts"]
    B --> C["forecast_demand"]
    C --> D["analyze_leave"]
    D --> E{"route_by_flow_type"}
    E -->|schedule| F["generate_schedule"]
    E -->|training| G["design_training"]
    E -->|hybrid| H["schedule + training"]
    E -->|shift_swap| I["coordinate_swap"]
    E -->|leave_review| J["leave_review"]
    F & G & H & I & J --> K["hitl_checkpoint"]
    K --> L["finalize"]

    style A fill:#4a9eff
    style B fill:#ff6b6b
    style C fill:#ff6b6b
    style D fill:#ff6b6b
    style F fill:#ff6b6b
    style G fill:#ff6b6b
    style H fill:#ff6b6b
    style I fill:#ff6b6b
    style K fill:#ffa500
    style L fill:#4a9eff
```
> 🔴 = LLM call (high latency) · 🟠 = HITL wait · 🔵 = local logic

---

## Identified Latency Sources

### 1. 🔴 Sequential LLM Calls (Dominant Bottleneck)

Every agent step creates a **new `Crew` object and calls `kickoff()`**, which triggers a full LLM round-trip. These run **strictly sequentially** due to the `@listen` chain in [bpo_flow.py](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py).

| Step | Agent | LLM Call? | Depends on previous? |
|------|-------|-----------|----------------------|
| [analyze_transcripts](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#130-150) | TranscriptAnalyzer | ✅ | Only [input_gatekeeper](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#69-128) |
| [forecast_demand](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#152-172) | DemandForecaster | ✅ | Needs `team_perf` from step above |
| [analyze_leave](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#174-208) | LeaveAnalyzer | ✅ | **Does NOT need** forecast output |
| [generate_schedule](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#226-232) | PerfAwareScheduler | ✅ | Needs forecast + leave + perf |
| [design_training](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#234-240) | TrainerDesigner | ✅ | Needs only `team_perf` |
| [coordinate_swap](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#254-270) | ShiftSwapCoordinator | ✅ | Needs only `leave_report` |

**Impact**: Each LLM call adds ~5–30s depending on model, prompt size, and API latency. For a [hybrid](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#242-252) flow (worst case), the pipeline makes **5 sequential LLM calls**, totaling **25–150s** of LLM wait time alone.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> [analyze_leave](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#174-208) does NOT depend on [forecast_demand](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#152-172) output — it only needs `queue_id` and `time_window`. Yet it waits for the forecast to complete due to the serial `@listen` chain.

---

### 2. 🟡 Serial MCP/Google Sheets Round-Trips

Each agent makes **1–2 separate MCP calls** to fetch data. These are HTTP round-trips to `mcp_server:8001`, which in turn makes Google Sheets API calls.

| Agent | MCP Calls | Data Fetched |
|-------|-----------|--------------|
| `transcript_analyzer` | 2 | [get_transcripts](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#264-321) + [get_agent_performance_data](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#376-428) |
| `demand_forecaster` | 1 | [get_historical_demand](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#430-485) |
| `leave_analyzer` | 1 | [get_agent_leave_data](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#323-374) |
| `perf_aware_scheduler` | 1 | [get_agent_availability](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#528-568) |
| `trainer_designer` | 1 | [get_course_catalog](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#487-526) |
| `shift_swap_coordinator` | 1 | [get_weekly_schedules](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/mcp_server/server.py#570-609) |

These calls happen **serially within each agent** and **serially across agents** — so 7 sequential HTTP+Google Sheets round-trips in a typical [schedule](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#226-232) flow.

**Impact**: Each Google Sheets API call takes ~200–800ms. Total: ~1.5–5.6s of serial I/O.

---

### 3. 🟡 Per-Call MCP Client Instantiation

In [mcp_client.py](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/utils/mcp_client.py#L70-L87), every [call_tool_sync()](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/utils/mcp_client.py#115-117) invocation:

1. Creates a **new [Client(MCP_SERVER_URL)](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/utils/mcp_client.py#112-120)** instance
2. Opens a **new HTTP connection** (`async with client:`)
3. Closes the connection after the call

```python
async def _call_tool_async(tool_name, arguments):
    client = Client(MCP_SERVER_URL)       # NEW client every call
    async with client:                     # NEW connection every call
        result = await client.call_tool(tool_name, arguments)
        return _parse_call_tool_result(result)
```

This adds **TCP/TLS handshake overhead** for every single MCP call.

---

### 4. 🟡 Synchronous MCP Calls from Async Context

The [call_tool_sync()](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/utils/mcp_client.py#115-117) wrapper uses `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` + `asyncio.run()` to bridge sync→async:

```python
future = _thread_pool.submit(asyncio.run, _call_tool_async(tool_name, arguments))
return future.result(timeout=60)
```

Each call creates a **new event loop** inside a thread, adding ~5–15ms overhead per call.

---

### 5. 🟠 Hardcoded Sleep Delays in API Layer

In [main.py](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/main.py#L186-L201):

```python
# Line 188: 3-second delay after HITL decision
time.sleep(3.0)  # Give finalize step time to complete

# Line 201: 1-second delay in _save_flow_to_db
time.sleep(1.0)
```

These are **unconditional waits** that add 1–4s of dead time to every flow completion.

---

### 6. 🟡 Hybrid Flow Runs Two LLM Agents Sequentially

In [bpo_flow.py L242-L251](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#L242-L251), [handle_hybrid()](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/flow/bpo_flow.py#242-252) runs schedule generation and training design **back-to-back**:

```python
def handle_hybrid(self):
    run_schedule_generation(self.state)   # LLM call #1
    run_training_design(self.state)       # LLM call #2 (waits for #1)
```

These two have **no data dependency** between each other — they both only need `team_perf`, [demand_forecast](file:///c:/Github%20Projects/crew-ai-hackathon-sama3a/backend/agents/demand_forecaster.py#47-164), and `leave_report` which are already computed by this point.

---

